From f79d2bdd0708a6b149c84c207429d81cd04add69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carl Kho <kho@uni.minerva.edu>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 08:58:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: bind ctrl+f to channel message search

Message search already existed but was reachable only through the header
button, so ctrl+f fell through to the browser find bar, which only sees the
messages currently rendered in the DOM.

Adds a CHAT_SEARCH keybind, an allowlist the handler consults so the native
find bar is suppressed for sequences the app fully replaces, and focus
handling for the search field. Also clears the pressed-key set when Meta is
released, since macOS withholds keyup for other keys while Command is held
and the stale key would fire the sequence on the next Command press.
